  "about": "Housed in the historic Domino Sugar Refinery, chef Missy Robbins’ Misi is a pasta-focused joint that keeps things simple. With just ten house-made pastas and ten antipasti plates, the James Beard-winning chef puts simple Italian cooking in the spotlight, highlighting seasonal ingredients. Take a seat at the bar, the kitchen counter, or the main dining room, and gorge yourself on some sheep’s milk ricotta-filled occhi.",
  "whyWeLikeIt": "Misi serves up some deceptively simple pastas, which are made fresh every morning. Be sure to peek inside the glass-enclosed pasta-making lab, and save room for dessert (spoiler alert: it’s gelato).",
  "needToKnow": null,
  "tagline": "Misi, located in South Williamsburg, Brooklyn, celebrates handmade pasta dishes and vegetable antipasti inspired by simple Italian cooking",
